.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_INJECT_NET_DGRAM 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_inject_net_dgram
.Nd inject a datagram as though received from the network
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_inject_net_dgram
.Fa "SSL *s"
.Fa "const unsigned char *buf"
.Fa "size_t buf_len"
.Fa "const BIO_ADDR *peer"
.Fa "const BIO_ADDR *local"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This function can be used to inject a datagram payload to a QUIC
connection SSL object.
The payload is processed as though it was received from the network.
This function can be used for debugging purposes or to allow datagrams
to be fed to QUIC from alternative sources.
.Pp
.Fa buf
is required and must point to a datagram payload to inject.
.Fa buf_len
is the length of the buffer in bytes.
The buffer is copied and need not remain valid after this function
returns.
.Pp
.Fa peer
and
.Fa local
are optional values pointing to
.Sy BIO_ADDR
structures describing the remote and local UDP endpoint addresses for
the packet.
Though the injected packet was not actually received from the network
directly by OpenSSL, the packet will be processed as though the received
datagram had the given addresses.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 1 on success or 0 on failure.
This function always fails if called on an SSL object which is not a
QUIC connection SSL object.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr OSSL_QUIC_client_method 3 ,
.Xr SSL_handle_events 3 ,
.Xr SSL_set_blocking_mode 3
.Sh HISTORY
The function
.Fn SSL_inject_net_dgram
was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
